 company operates fleet maintenance centers. As of December 31, 2025, it owned and operated 10,184 tractors, 30,824 linehaul trailers, and 14,313 pickup and delivery trailers. Old Dominion Freight Line, Inc. was founded in 1934 and is headquartered in Thomasville, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin M. Freeman | President, CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $9.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $272K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $637 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 34\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Old Dominion Freight Line, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $34.0B market cap on $5.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 33% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 23-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $955M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.34\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage 